Q: Deduced conflicting types for parameter const T (unsigned char and int) A: <p>(My) Answer from first &quot;potential duplicates&quot; fixes your issue:</p>
<pre><code>template &lt;class T&gt;
const T&amp; clamp (const T&amp; value,
                std::type_identity_t&lt;const T&amp;&gt; low,
                std::type_identity_t&lt;const T&amp;&gt; high)
{
    return (value &lt; low ? low : (value &gt; high ? high : value));
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://godbolt.org/z/eacaeeWP3" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
<p><code>T</code> is only deduced from <code>value</code>. <code>low</code>/<code>high</code> will use the same <code>T</code>.</p>
